-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Exemption) Order (G.N. No. S 307/1996; O 1, 2004 Revised Edition, amended by S 600/2014), made under s 60 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-order-1996/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-OR1.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- It exempts the PROVISION of the listed services from ss 8 and 9 (the licensing of services); it says nothing about apparatus. Dated: the window of the Order as deposited.

§ `Paragraph 1: Exemption of the provision of listed services from sections 8 and 9`

-- src:2 | 1. The Minister for Information, Communications and the Arts has exempted in relation to the provision of the following services, any person who provides any of the following services from sections 8 and 9 of the Broadcasting Act:
-- src:3 | ( a ) news wire services where the information is transmitted primarily for the purposes of news-gathering by broadcasting or newspaper companies;
-- src:4 | ( b ) financial information services where the financial information is transmitted without commentary and without alteration or addition to its form;
-- src:5 | ( c ) weather or traffic news services;
-- src:6 | ( d ) close circuit television surveillance services that are —
-- src:7 | (i) transmitted for reception within the confines of a single building, dwelling-house, hospital, educational institution, residential, commercial or industrial complex, or any single temporary or permanent structure; and
-- src:8 | (ii) provided solely for the purpose of security surveillance;
-- src:9 | ( e ) airline in-flight entertainment and information services that are provided on aircraft;
-- src:10 | ( f ) computer on-line services other than computer on-line services subject to a class licence under the Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (N 1) or subject to a notice under paragraph 3A(1) of that Notification; or
-- src:12 | ( g ) other licensable broadcasting services that are regulated or licensed by the Government, or a statutory authority, under any written law.
@ref para 1(a) to (g) (src:2-12)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `it is a news wire service where the information is transmitted primarily for news-gathering by broadcasting or newspaper companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a financial information service where the financial information is transmitted without commentary and without alteration or addition to its form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a weather or traffic news service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a close circuit television surveillance service transmitted for reception within the confines of a single building, dwelling-house, hospital, educational institution, residential, commercial or industrial complex, or single temporary or permanent structure, and provided solely for security surveillance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an airline in-flight entertainment and information service provided on aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a computer on-line service that is not subject to a class licence under the Class Licence Notification or to a notice under paragraph 3A(1) of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another licensable broadcasting service regulated or licensed by the Government, or a statutory authority, under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`O 1 para 1 the person who provides the service is exempt from sections 8 and 9 of the Act, on` MEANS
    IF `the Exemption Order of 1996 as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`it is a news wire service where the information is transmitted primarily for news-gathering by broadcasting or newspaper companies`
        OR `it is a financial information service where the financial information is transmitted without commentary and without alteration or addition to its form`
        OR `it is a weather or traffic news service`
        OR `it is a close circuit television surveillance service transmitted for reception within the confines of a single building, dwelling-house, hospital, educational institution, residential, commercial or industrial complex, or single temporary or permanent structure, and provided solely for security surveillance`
        OR `it is an airline in-flight entertainment and information service provided on aircraft`
        OR `it is a computer on-line service that is not subject to a class licence under the Class Licence Notification or to a notice under paragraph 3A(1) of it`
        OR `it is another licensable broadcasting service regulated or licensed by the Government, or a statutory authority, under a written law`)
    ELSE NOTHING

